    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0397" n="1151" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/89a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-03T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>811. After consultation with McCormick it has been decided negotiations of
                    agreement with Holland should be carried on in London. McCormick returning from
                    Paris this week to take up this question with British and French and will try to
                    reach some understanding.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
